                <pb facs="0178" n="169" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg169"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/1539b: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-15T18:00:00-05:00">October 15, 1940—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2731. Department is contemplating the dispatch of the S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt</hi> to Galway or some other
                    practicable western or southern port in Ireland to evacuate additional Americans
                    in the <pb facs="0179" n="170" xml:id="pg170"/> British Isles to the United
                    States. The ship will carry no cargo or passengers on its outward journey from
                    the United States. Please immediately communicate informally to the appropriate
                    German authorities and ascertain whether the German Government would be willing
                    to grant safe conduct for the vessel on its voyage for the purpose stated. If
                    so, this Government will instruct you formally to request safe conduct. It will
                    then also state the date of sailing of the ship, the course to be followed by it
                    to Ireland and the probable date of arrival in Ireland. The vessel will, of
                    course, proceed with the usual identifying characteristics as on its previous
                    voyage to Galway. Telegraph reply triple priority.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
